I get into the taxi.
It is nicely warm in the taxi.
"Good evening," the driver says.
"Where are we driving to?"
"Good evening," I answer.
"To Schillerstraße, please."
We drive off.
There is a lot of traffic on the street.
"Are you from Berlin?" the driver asks.
"No, I am new here," I say.
"My name is Maya."
"Where do you come from?" he asks politely.
"I come from Mexico."
"How nice," he says.
"What do you do in Berlin?"
"I am a software engineer," I explain.
"I work here now."
The driver smiles in the mirror.
"Then welcome to Berlin!"
"Thank you very much," I say.
